# shellcheck configuration for `make lint-shell` (issue #122).
#
# THIS FILE IS A HOLE IN A GATE, so it is deliberately one line long and carries its reason. The
# rule test/repo/lint_shell_test.go enforces is that the disable list stays exactly what is argued
# for below: TestShellcheckRC_DisablesOnlyTheArguedRule fails on a second id, so widening this is a
# reviewed act and not a quiet way to make a diagnostic go away. Everything else runs at
# shellcheck's DEFAULT severity — style, which is to say all of it — because raising the severity to
# `warning` would drop SC2086, and SC2086 is precisely the defect (#111) that bought this gate.
#
# SC2016 — "expressions don't expand in single quotes".
#
# Every hit in this repository is the same shape and every one is correct:
#
#     printf '  run `make setup` first\n'
#
# A printf FORMAT string is single-quoted here as a matter of course — that is what keeps a `%` or a
# backslash in it from being re-interpreted, and every value that must expand is passed as an
# argument to `%s` rather than interpolated into the format. shellcheck reads the markdown backticks
# in the prose as legacy command substitution and reports the format string. Eight such messages
# exist across scripts/ and .githooks/, all of them user-facing instructions.
#
# The alternative was eight `# shellcheck disable=SC2016` comments sitting above eight printf lines
# that are not wrong, which teaches the reader that a disable comment means nothing. One reasoned
# exception in a file whose whole subject is the exception is the more honest version.
#
# What this does NOT waive: SC2086 (word splitting — #111), SC2015 and SC2251 (the `a && b || c`
# shape that made #84's readyz probe assert nothing), or anything else. Those are the rules the gate
# was bought for.
disable=SC2016
